827	# handoffs/NN-codex-<ReplyName>-<provider>.md and ledger entry with the `panel` record. A
828	# member that fails or is refused does not stop the others - unless it leaves surviving
829	# processes: they hold the task's reservation, so the remaining members are not started
830	# (recorded in the summary as skipped, exit 1). This run itself takes no lock
831	# and writes nothing; it prints a summary and exits 0 only when every member produced a
832	# usable reply (-DryRun: when every member's plan could be made).
