4286	# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- task lock + pending record
4287	#
4288	# OWNERSHIP and RECOVERY METADATA are two different files:
4289	#
4290	#   <task>/.consult.lock          ownership. A PERMANENT file at a stable path: opened
4291	#                                 with FileMode.OpenOrCreate and held open for the whole
4292	#                                 critical section; release = close the handle, never
4293	#                                 unlink (a contender that already opened the path must
4294	#                                 never end up locking a different file than the next
4295	#                                 one). The OS decides ownership: a holder that dies
4296	#                                 loses it with its handle. Share mode:
4297	#                                   * Windows: FileShare.Read - a refused contender can
4298	#                                     read the holder's record for its message, nobody
4299	#                                     else can open it for writing;
4300	#                                   * elsewhere: FileShare.None, which .NET on Unix
4301	#                                     emulates with an advisory flock(LOCK_EX) (any other
4302	#                                     share mode maps to a shared lock that would not
4303	#                                     exclude).
4304	#                                 Cross-host exclusion (a task directory on a network
4305	#                                 share used from two machines) is out of scope. The
4306	#                                 content is informational only - { pid, start_time,
4307	#                                 host, task, started } of the current holder - written
4308	#                                 after the handle is held; overwriting it destroys
4309	#                                 nothing recoverable.
4310	#
4311	#   <task>/.consult.pending.json  recovery metadata of the consultation in progress,
4312	#                                 replaced ATOMICALLY (Write-TextAtomic) and only while
4313	#                                 the lock is held:
4314	#                                   { state, n, nn, reply, started, pid, host, launcher,
4315	#                                     child_pid, child_start_time, survivors, note }
4316	#                                 state: reserved   numbers allocated, codex not started
4317	#                                        launching  about to start codex (the child may
4318	#                                                   or may not exist)
4319	#                                        running    codex started as child_pid
4320	#                                        survivors  a timeout kill left survivors[] alive
4321	#                                 pid: the bridge that wrote the record. survivors[]:
4322	#                                   { pid, start_time, name } per process still alive
4323	#                                   after the kill (start_time: UTC round-trip string
4324	#                                   from Get-Process; name: its ProcessName). A recorded
4325	#                                   process counts as alive only while its pid runs with
4326	#                                   the SAME start time (and name, when recorded); an
4327	#                                   entry without a start time (older records: a bare
4328	#                                   pid) counts only if that process looks like codex
4329	#                                   (Test-RecordedProcess) - never by pid alone.
4330	#                                 It is deleted when the run completed cleanly (after the
4331	#                                 ledger commit). A run that finds one decides from it
4332	#                                 BEFORE writing anything (Test-PendingActive): a live
4333	#                                 codex process refuses the run; a dead one's reservation
4334	#                                 is consumed (numbering skips past it) and only then is
4335	#                                 the file replaced by the new run's record. An
4336	#                                 unparseable pending file is corruption and refuses.
4337	
4338	# Process start time as a UTC round-trip string. $null: no such process. '': the
4339	# process exists but its start time cannot be read (e.g. another user's process).
4340	function Get-ProcessStartIso {
4341	    param([int]$ProcessId)
4342	    $p = $null
4343	    try { $p = Get-Process -Id $ProcessId -ErrorAction Stop } catch { return $null }
4344	    try { return $p.StartTime.ToUniversalTime().ToString('o', $script:Invariant) } catch { return '' }
4345	}
